message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Forcing admission under evidence gates: which phytochemical screen scores may enter a tip ODE as known forcings?"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  When a phytochemical screen is barred from writing scores into Theta,
  which of those scores — if any — may be admitted as declared known
  forcings into a tip ODE without bypassing evidence gates or leaking
  through soft priors? Twelve claim records transcribed from Thesis #16
  are tested by an admission ledger. Seventeen calls return refused.
  One call admits a protocol-constant forcing schedule for row L10.
  The SHA-256 of the kinetic vector is unchanged under the refusals and
  under that admission. The state path moves because the forcing moved.
  Not a medical device. No efficacy claim. No document DOI.
keywords:
  - evidence gates
  - forcing admission
  - kinetic parameters
  - phytochemical screen
  - ordinary differential equations
  - soft prior
  - ledger
  - research-only
